      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the turbine blade wash is an inherent part of turbocharger operation, there are ways to reduce the noise.Research has led to the development of engineered blades and stator vanes that minimize blade beat frequencies, leading to a quieter turbo operation. Additionally, many current modern turbochargers incorporate sound-dampening materials and active noise cancellation techniques to reduce the noise level. However, these modifications often come at the expense of slightly reduced efficiency, but the overall effect can still achieve a noticeable reduction in noise.",
